Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: enforce bridge port policy before fallback binding

A known destination can resolve back to the ingress port. Do not bind
that path unless bridge hairpin is enabled. Resolve physical ingress
through VLAN and br_netfilter contexts and reject unknown or disabled
bridge ports. Ordinary cross-port and permitted wireless hairpin paths
continue to use PPE. Add an RCU-safe STP reader for the RX path,
preserving the existing RTNL-only bridge API.

This file was generated entirely by AI.
It has not been reviewed line by line by a human.

